FBCL-Net: Feature-Based Contrastive Learning Network for EEG Music Classification
Overview

FBCL-Net (Feature-Based Contrastive Learning Network) is a deep learning framework developed for classifying music stimuli from EEG (Electroencephalography) signals. The model combines handcrafted EEG features, attention mechanisms, contrastive learning, CNN-LSTM architectures, and multi-branch feature encoders to improve classification performance.

The system processes EEG recordings collected while subjects listen to different songs and predicts the corresponding song class based on extracted brain activity patterns.

Features
EEG preprocessing using MNE
Automatic feature extraction from EEG epochs
Multi-band frequency analysis
Band Attention Module
Multi-Branch Feature Encoders
CNN-LSTM Temporal Encoder
Supervised Contrastive Learning
Class-balanced training
Attention visualization
t-SNE embedding visualization
Performance comparison plots
Dataset Structure

The notebook expects EEG data organized as:

dataset/
│
├── sub-01/
│   ├── ses-01/
│   │   └── eeg/
│   │       └── *.set
│   ├── ses-02/
│   └── ...
│
├── sub-02/
├── sub-03/
└── ...

Supported EEG file formats:

.set
.fif
.edf
.bdf
EEG Preprocessing

The preprocessing pipeline includes:

Loading EEG files
Selecting EEG channels
Average referencing
Band-pass filtering (1–50 Hz)
Notch filtering at 50 Hz
Epoch generation

Configuration:

EPOCH_SEC = 4.0
OVERLAP_SEC = 2.0

Each EEG recording is divided into overlapping epochs for training.

Frequency Bands Used
Band	Frequency Range
Delta	1 – 4 Hz
Theta	4 – 8 Hz
Alpha	8 – 13 Hz
Beta	13 – 30 Hz
Gamma	30 – 50 Hz
Feature Extraction

For each EEG epoch, the following features are extracted.

Frequency-Domain Features
Delta Band Power
Theta Band Power
Alpha Band Power
Beta Band Power
Gamma Band Power
Band Ratios
Theta / Alpha
Alpha / Beta
Statistical Features
Mean
Standard Deviation
Skewness
Kurtosis
Peak-to-Peak Amplitude
Hjorth Parameters
Activity
Mobility
Complexity
Feature Groups

The extracted features are divided into four semantic groups:

Feature Group	Description
Band Power	EEG frequency band powers
Ratios	Theta/Alpha and Alpha/Beta ratios
Time Statistics	Statistical characteristics
Hjorth Parameters	Signal complexity measures
FBCL-Net Architecture
1. Band Attention Module

The Band Attention Module learns which EEG frequency bands contribute most to classification.

Input:

(Batch Size, 5 Bands, Channels)

Output:

Weighted EEG representation

Advantages:

Learns important frequency bands automatically
Improves interpretability
Generates attention scores for visualization
2. Multi-Branch Feature Encoders

Each feature group is processed independently.

Branches:

Band Power Encoder
Ratio Encoder
Time Statistics Encoder
Hjorth Encoder

Each branch contains:

Fully Connected Layers
Layer Normalization
GELU Activation
Residual Connections
Dropout

Output:

Fixed-length embeddings
3. CNN-LSTM Temporal Encoder

The temporal branch captures long-range EEG dependencies.

Components:

CNN Layers
1D Convolutions
Residual Blocks
Batch Normalization
GELU Activations
LSTM Layers
Bidirectional LSTM
Two Layers
Temporal Feature Learning

Benefits:

Captures local patterns using CNN
Captures temporal dynamics using LSTM
4. Feature Fusion

Outputs from:

Band Attention Module
Feature Encoders
CNN-LSTM Temporal Encoder

are fused into a shared latent representation.

5. Classification Head

The fused representation is passed through fully connected layers to predict song classes.

Output:

12 Song Classes
Supervised Contrastive Learning

FBCL-Net incorporates Supervised Contrastive Loss to improve feature discrimination.

Objectives:

Pull same-class embeddings closer
Push different-class embeddings apart
Improve generalization

Combined Loss:

Total Loss =
Cross Entropy Loss +
λ × Contrastive Loss

where:

λ = 0.3
Training Configuration
Optimizer
AdamW

Learning Rate:

3e-4

Weight Decay:

1e-4
Scheduler

Cosine Learning Rate Decay with Warmup

Batch Sizes
Train Batch Size = 128
Validation Batch Size = 256
Training Epochs
120 Epochs
Early Stopping

Patience:

20 Epochs
